		{
			"id": "Tickets",
			"_note": "The tickets list in the simple structure (openspec/changes/simple-contact-dashboard). No view is dropped: the four the page had keep their filter and gain a count, three join them, five show and the rest sit behind the overflow chip. `Waiting for me`, `New` and `Waiting for customer` use the same filters as the dashboard stats that link here. THE AVATAR IS THE HANDLER'S: `assignee` holds a Nextcloud user id. The design draws the customer's initials, and a ticket holds its client as a reference without a name. THE COLOUR IS ON THE DEADLINE: late or due today is red (`lte 0`), due within two days is amber. How long a ticket has waited cannot be coloured, a date rule counts days until a date and a wait lies in the past.",
			"config": {
				"quickFilterMaxVisible": 6,
				"columns": [
					{
						"key": "title",
						"label": "Subject"
					},
					{
						"key": "ticketType",
						"label": "Type"
					},
					{
						"key": "status",
						"label": "Status",
						"widget": "statusBadge"
					},
					"channel",
